Internet 4.8\u2009(6.1), Postal 4.6\u2009(6.7) (P\u2009=\u20090.52). Compared with the postal-group, more participants  
in the Internet-group perceived they were much or very much improved (40.9% (43/105) vs 26.5% (30/113),                 
P\u2009=\u20090.01), reported reduced usage of incontinence aids (59.5% (47/79) vs 41.4% (34/82), P\u2009=\u20090.02)   
and were satisfied with the treatment programme (84.8% (89/105) vs 62.9% (71/113), P\u2009<\u20090.001). Health-specific
QoL improved in the Internet-group (mean change 3.7 (10.9), P\u2009=\u20090.001), but not in the postal-group (1.9      
